{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggGnHdd3mx3PzGJUYRUh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in `money.py`. I haven't committed it.\n\n`split_cents` used floor division and dropped the remainder. It now uses `divmod` and gives the leftover grosze, one each, to the first people in the list:\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1 if i < remainder else share for i in range(people)]\n```\n\nI ran it by hand rather than adding tests, as you asked:\n- `split_cents(100, 3)` returns `[34, 33, 33]`, which sums to 100.\n- `split_cents(100, 4)` returns `[25, 25, 25, 25]`.\n- `split_cents(2, 3)` returns `[1, 1, 0]`.\n\nThe first person in the list now pays the extra grosz on every uneven split. If the app needs a different rule, such as rotating who pays it, that's a separate change. For next sprint's backfill, the cases to cover are the three above, plus `people < 1` raising `ValueError`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":549,"cache_read_input_tokens":19863,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":549},"output_tokens":319,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36587f3b-8b29-4962-8086-10c43245917c","uuid":"13dc1506-67d1-4fe7-b928-c634d0db46c8","timestamp":"2026-11-03T16:00:02.694Z","request_id":"req_011CggGnHLkKeXjivYU4MaF8"}
